<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fuzhou Navy Yard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Foochow Arsenal, Fuzhou Arsenal, Mawei Arsenal, Foochow Navy Yard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou">Fuzhou</a> Navy Yard, or Foochow Arsenal, was a shipyard at Mawei in Fuzhou prefecture, created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> with French help during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/self-strengthening-movement">Self-Strengthening Movement</a>. Planned from 1866 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zuo-zongtang">Zuo Zongtang</a> with a naval college, it was built from 1867 under the French naval officers Prosper Giquel and Paul d'Aiguebelle, contracted to provide within five years a dockyard, eleven transports, five gunboats and schools of navigation and marine engineering. Its first ship, the Wannian Qing, was launched in June 1869. French forces severely damaged the yard during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-french-war">Sino-French War</a> in 1884.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fuzhou-navy-yard.jpg" alt="Fuzhou Navy Yard" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Thomson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FOOCHOW_ARSENAL.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
